image crate (perceptual image hashing, `vision` feature only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Copyright (c) the image-rs project contributors (https://github.com/image-rs).

    Source location: https://github.com/image-rs/image

    `crates/pdf2md-core` has an opt-in `vision` cargo feature (enabled for the
    commercial-server build, not for the public/WASM defaults) that uses the Rust
    `image` crate (0.25.x, dual MIT / Apache-2.0) plus its PNG and JPEG codec
    dependencies to compute 64-bit DCT perceptual hashes of page rasters. These
    hashes let the commercial Vision-rescue layer recognise a repeated form and
    serve a cached result instead of re-invoking the LLM. All such dependencies
    are permissively licensed (MIT / Apache-2.0 / Zlib); see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.
